   "body": "### Mac check (mac/verify-merges, 2026-11-02)\nSimulator, iOS 27.0, iPhone 18 Pro and iPad Pro 13-inch (M5). The build is dev-swift `34c4e556`, then the same build with #377. A local XCUITest driver ran the checks (not committed). Login used the operator's capture account, read-only.\n\n| Row | iPhone | iPad | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1a (session invalid, account kept) | ⚪ not triggerable | ⚪ not triggerable | I found no way, by hand on the simulator, to make HFR refuse the *same* `HFRSession` while the account stays. Logging out and removing the account both replace the object. The unit tests `aSessionThatExpiresClosesTheOpenConversation` and `aRefusedSessionClosesTheOpenConversationEvenWithItsCookie` stand alone. |\n| 1b (remove account) | ✅ pass | ✅ pass | Log in, Messages, open a conversation (reader web view shown). Then Plus/sidebar > account menu > Gérer les comptes… > Retirer. Result: Messages shows only the signed-out list (\"Connexion requise\"), with no row and no reader. On iPad the detail column shows \"Choisissez une conversation\". The app has no separate log-out action, so removal is the only way to log out. No screenshot, because the conversation is private. |\n| 2 (Plus > Réglages > Icône) | ❌ **fail on `34c4e556`** → ✅ with #377 | ✅ pass | On iPhone the Icône and Thème rows highlighted and pushed nothing. The cause came with #303: Réglages is presented by `navigationDestination(item:)`, and a value link pushed from it never resolves. #377 fixes it with direct links, merged as `1c5cd6f`. With #377: Icône, back, twice; Catégories and back keeps Réglages; back pops to Plus. Screenshots: [344-1](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/docs/mac-checks-344-322/docs/assets/checks/344-1.png), [344-2](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/docs/mac-checks-344-322/docs/assets/checks/344-2.png). |\n\nEvery row that can be checked passes on the current head. 1a is left to its unit tests, as this issue allows. The screenshots are in PR #381, which closes this issue once merged, and that unblocks LOT-161 (#251).\n",
   "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
